WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.410
Edinburgh, 1910.

2
00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:06.920
Delegates from Western churches meet
to plan the spread of Christianity.

3
00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:11.780
They picture mission as going from the
Christian West to the non-Christian world.

4
00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:15.850
Mission ran one way: from
the West, to the rest.

5
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:20.170
Today, churches founded in Africa
have congregations in Britain.

6
00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:24.040
So why do some Christians now
come to Britain to do the same?

7
00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:29.040
In this mission, you'll trace how
ideas of mission changed after 1910.

8
00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:34.500
Then you'll weigh up whether mission still
fits a society of many faiths and none.

9
00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:39.810
Your mission: find out why Christians from
former mission fields now come to Britain.
